1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,680
You're shot in the chest in 1912.

2
00:00:03,290 --> 00:00:05,370
You refuse the hospital and speak for 50

3
00:00:05,370 --> 00:00:07,400
minutes. So why aren't you dead?

4
00:00:07,732 --> 00:00:10,822
October 14, 1912. Milwaukee.

5
00:00:11,392 --> 00:00:13,692
Former President Teddy Roosevelt is campaigning

6
00:00:13,692 --> 00:00:15,042
for the White House.

7
00:00:15,311 --> 00:00:18,111
Outside his hotel, a man named John Schrank

8
00:00:18,111 --> 00:00:20,001
fires one shot into his chest.

9
00:00:20,371 --> 00:00:22,111
But the bullet first tears through a steel

10
00:00:22,111 --> 00:00:23,971
glasses case, and his speech,

11
00:00:23,971 --> 00:00:26,861
folded in half. 50 pages thick.

12
00:00:27,126 --> 00:00:28,316
He coughs into his hand.

13
00:00:28,526 --> 00:00:30,376
No blood. So the lung is fine.

14
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:31,750
He walks on stage.

15
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:33,740
"I don't know whether you fully understand

16
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:35,230
that I have just been shot.

17
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:37,580
But it takes more than that to kill a Bull

18
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:38,270
Moose."

19
00:00:38,444 --> 00:00:39,854
He speaks for 50 minutes,

20
00:00:40,004 --> 00:00:41,574
blood seeping into his shirt.

21
00:00:42,144 --> 00:00:43,354
Then he goes to the hospital.

22
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:46,610
An X-ray finds it lodged in his chest muscle.

23
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:48,170
Doctors leave it there.

24
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:50,090
He carried it for the rest of his life.

25
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:51,810
Would you have walked on stage?

26
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:52,910
Tell me below.

